# Larger action icons within the existing tile
Workstream-ID: lea-35
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/35
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed bounded public desktop presentation request
Status: DONE
Milestone: Enlarge every action icon while preserving the original tile dimensions
Dependencies: lea-33, lea-34

## Purpose
Make all 36 action icons easier to see without enlarging the 112-by-108 logical
pixel tile. Use the selected 64-by-64 icon size while retaining complete action
names, their existing rounded font, semantic colors and steady border glow.

## Tasks
- [x] Measure the original tile and every label in both desktop themes.
- [x] Establish an isolated source candidate with fictional test workspaces.
- [x] Enlarge the rendered vectors and displayed icon widgets together.
- [x] Verify all states, display densities and compact/expanded layouts.
- [x] Refresh directly affected documentation and fictional Run media.
- [x] Deliver the qualified source change without controlling independent apps.
- [x] Reconcile the scoped issue, Project status and persistent backlink.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Every action uses a 64-by-64 logical pixel icon, not just a denser bitmap.
- [x] The tile remains exactly 112-by-108 logical pixels for every state.
- [x] Full labels retain their font, size, colors and accessible descriptions.
- [x] Icon and name remain centered, separated and contained without clipping.
- [x] High-density rendering, retained resume and neighboring controls still work.
- [x] README media and affected guides accurately distinguish source from releases.
- [x] One issue-backed Project item and durable backlink represent this workstream.
- [x] Private setup, predecessor work, independent apps and releases are preserved.

## Completion evidence
Initial isolated measurements cover all 36 states in both themes at minimum
and expanded window sizes: the original tile is 112 by 108 logical pixels and
its icons are 40 by 40. Two-line labels need 28 pixels, so an 80-by-80 icon
cannot retain those labels and padding inside the existing tile. The selected
64-by-64 size preserves the box while increasing icon area by 2.56 times.

Both the displayed widget and density-aware vector render target now use 64
logical pixels. Five-pixel margins and four-pixel spacing preserve the exact
original tile, complete centered labels and unchanged Nunito font. The artwork,
semantic colors/glow, accessible descriptions and retained resume behavior remain
unchanged. All 144 state/theme/layout comparisons retain exact tile positions,
neighboring console geometry, label dimensions and font size without clipping.

All 83 GUI cases pass, as do focused Ruff, Black and mypy checks. A separate
double-scale execution passes eight affected cases. Seven guides, seven fictional
Run screenshots and the nine-frame Run GIF are refreshed; all 148 relative
references resolve and all 36 glossary exports remain unchanged. Direct visual
review covers before/after Ready and two-line Preparing application in both
themes, the GIF's first frame and the compact light Run view, not every frame.

Exactly eighteen qualified source/test/documentation/media files are delivered
and byte-verified in the original checkout. Eight focused original-source GUI
cases pass; actual imports resolve to that checkout and the unchanged source
launcher's nonlaunching check passes. All 249 baseline files outside the payload
and three deliberate tracking edits retain exact bytes and modification times.
Final scoped issue/Project/backlink reconciliation is recorded in the index
and development ledger.

This is local technical completion, not live LinkedIn qualification, human
acceptance or publication. Published v0.2.4 and installed applications are
unchanged. No application restart, commit, push or new release is included.

